WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.600
dopamine the brain's pleasure signal?

2
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.620
It is a common shortcut.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.520
Let's test it.

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.870
Two things need separating.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.050
Wanting is the pull of a reward and its cues.

6
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.150
Liking is the pleasure of the reward itself.

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.920
How can you measure liking in a rat, without asking?

8
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
Watch its face.

9
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.750
Sweet tastes bring tongue protrusions.

10
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.870
Bitter tastes bring gapes.

11
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.430
These reactions can be scored from video.

12
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.400
Rats whose forebrain dopamine was depleted with a neurotoxin stopped seeking food.

13
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:43.053
If dopamine carried pleasure, what should their faces do when sugar is placed in the

14
00:00:43.053 --> 00:00:44.053
mouth?

15
00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.787
Their faces showed normal liking reactions.

16
00:00:52.607 --> 00:00:55.527
The seeking was gone, but the liking reactions remained.

17
00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:57.907
Now the other direction.

18
00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:03.847
Mutant mice make little of the dopamine transporter, so extra dopamine stays outside

19
00:01:03.847 --> 00:01:04.847
the cells.

20
00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.387
They reached sweet food sooner in a runway.

21
00:01:08.407 --> 00:01:09.407
They ran no faster.

22
00:01:10.207 --> 00:01:11.667
They just paused less on the way.

23
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.540
But their liking reactions to sugar were no stronger.

24
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:20.053
So, in these tests, dopamine moved wanting, not liking.

25
00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:23.066
Recall the burst that moves to cues.

26
00:01:24.026 --> 00:01:28.266
It is compatible with cues gaining pull, but whether it is wanting is debated.

27
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:35.390
Keep the scope. A lifelong mutation is not an acute drug, and an animal's face is

28
00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.390
not a human report.

29
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.280
Other researchers read the same results as changes in willingness to work, or in

30
00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.280
learning.

31
00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:47.253
Addictive drugs raise dopamine signalling, by different routes.

32
00:01:48.183 --> 00:01:53.663
Incentive sensitization theory proposes that in susceptible people, repeated use can

33
00:01:53.663 --> 00:01:55.243
make cue-triggered wanting grow.

34
00:01:56.043 --> 00:01:57.863
It can grow out of proportion to liking.

35
00:01:58.966 --> 00:02:02.846
It offers one explanation for why craving can outlast enjoyment.

36
00:02:03.706 --> 00:02:05.806
It is a theory, and other accounts exist.

37
00:02:07.016 --> 00:02:10.296
In these tests, dopamine moved wanting, not liking.

38
00:02:11.216 --> 00:02:15.496
Its quick bursts mark better than predicted, and its pauses worse than predicted.

39
00:02:16.376 --> 00:02:18.116
They are not a direct measure of pleasure.
